From d731f595945af91e244f9c54c6e6ab0ab2d1b275 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:57:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(v2): alias stored tool parts to the v1 shape and stop the
 transcript retry loop

OpenCode 2 stores an assistant tool call as { type: "tool", id, name,
state } (session_message rows on 2.0.32). The v1 hook code reads the
OpenCode 1 fields `tool` and `callID`, so on the v2 session facade every
PostToolUse transcript build hit transformToolName(undefined), threw
TypeError, and logged "[transcript] failed to build transcript from
session {"error":{}}" because JSON.stringify drops an Error's message.
The failure never populated the transcript cache, so each tool call read
the whole session history again and failed again: 6,924 identical lines
in %TEMP%/oh-my-opencode.log between 2026-10-16 and 2026-10-19, plus
1,630 "failed to clean up previous temp transcript" ENOENT lines from the
cache still pointing at the file the hook runner had just deleted.

- storedMessagesToV1 now adds `tool` (from name) and `callID` (from id)
  to tool parts of the read-only session view. The hook message view that
  is written back to the host is unchanged.
- The transcript reads `tool` or `name`, skips a part with neither, logs
  errors with name/message/code, remembers a failed history fetch for one
  minute instead of re-fetching on every tool call, and forgets a temp
  transcript that deleteTempTranscript removed.
